"4" direction="1">0</POWER><LABEL pos="158,111.03125" font="5" color="208000" direction="1" style="0">PWM</LABEL><LABEL pos="164,112.765625" font="5" color="208000" direction="1" style="0">DIR</LABEL><LABEL pos="134,111.421875" font="5" color="208000" direction="1" style="0">ENABLE</LABEL><POWER pos="140,118" which="4" direction="1">0</POWER><POWER pos="108,160" which="0" direction="0">VMOTOR</POWER><POWER pos="116,184" which="4" direction="1">0</POWER><POWER pos="39,180" which="4" direction="1">0</POWER><LABEL pos="47,174.4390625" font="5" color="208000" direction="1" style="0">LIMIT_NC</LABEL><NOTE_TEXT a="202,128" b="280,182" font="5" color="453626" style="4" fill="0" direction="3" border_style="2">Matching labels join control nets.GPIO18: PWMGPIO19: directionGPIO25: enableGPIO27: NC limit, input pull-upCommon 0 is the signal return.</NOTE_TEXT><NOTE_TEXT a="20,200" b="280,208" font="5" color="453626" style="4" fill="0" direction="3" border_style="2">Use a 3.3V-compatible driver and matching motor/supply ratings. Firmware starts disabled and stops on an open NC limit.This is a wiring layout, with no firmware, motion simulation or certified emergency-stop function. See Explanation.</NOTE_TEXT></TinyCAD><DSNSETTINGS><SHOW_RULERS>1</SHOW_RULERS></DSNSETTINGS><NETLIST_TYPES><TYPE name="default"/></NETLIST_TYPES></TinyCADSheets>